    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T14:30:02Z",
    "body": "Decided by the maintainer (2026-11-13, in chat): \"That test and cut runner should be linux and it can only run on self hosted agents\".\n\nWhat that settles:\n\n- **Runner:** the gate and cut jobs run on Linux, on self-hosted runners only (`runs-on: [self-hosted, linux]`); never on GitHub-hosted runners.\n- **Actions budget:** self-hosted runners use no billed minutes, so the 3000-minute budget does not limit this workflow. `release.yml` (the publishing build) is unchanged by this decision.\n\nWhat it opens:\n\n- **Windows-only readings.** Some tests pin per-OS values (the adaptive-roughing move counts of issue 1402 have a Windows arm and a Linux arm). A Linux gate checks only the Linux arm; say in the PR whether Windows values are still checked locally at a cut or are left to drift.\n- **UI snapshot lane on Linux.** The pixel goldens were made on Windows; the PR says whether the lane runs on the Linux runner (own goldens, or a GPU-less render) or stays a local step.\n- **Runner safety.** A self-hosted runner executes the workflow's code on the maintainer's machine: keep the trigger `workflow_dispatch` only, never `pull_request` (a fork PR must not be able to run code there), and say in AGENTS.md how the runner is registered and labelled.\n- **Runner setup** is part of \"Done means\": the toolchain, sccache and disk the runner needs are written down.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
